  "operation": "verify_password",
  "conformance_level": "MUST",
  "spec_section": "docs/identity.md#lifecycle",
  "description": "User status is honoured at authentication and issuance time (ADR 0029; `docs/identity.md` \u00a7Lifecycle): no operation that authenticates a principal, or issues something that will later authenticate one, succeeds for a non-`active` user. Every refusal arm is paired with a reinstate-and-succeed arm (the known positive: suspension is reversible, so the gate is evaluated at verify/issue time, not by cascade). ERROR NAMES (pinned by ADR 0029's table): `verifyPassword` \u2192 `InvalidCredentialError` (no user-status oracle); `createSession` and `createPat` \u2192 `PreconditionError`; `verifyPatToken` for a suspended owner \u2192 `InvalidPatTokenError` (conflated, so status is not disclosed); a PAT revoked with its owner \u2192 `PatRevokedError` (ADR 0016). `verifyMfa` \u2192 `InvalidCredentialError` (conflated with proof failure). The `verify_mfa` vectors use the same harness pseudo-ops as `identity/mfa/totp-replay-rejected.json` (`set_clock`, `compute_totp_code`) with `enroll_totp_factor` / `confirm_totp_factor`. NOT asserted in this file: the `refreshSession` and `verifySessionToken` arms ADR 0029 lists, which need harness ops not yet in the fixture vocabulary (`refresh_session`, `verify_session_token`). PAT CASCADE: the vector asserts ADR 0016 \u00a7Constraints' behaviour ('PATs auto-revoke when their owner is revoked'); the text is inconsistent about WHERE the cascade lives (0016 names `cascadeRevokeSubject`, which authorization.md defines as a tuple delete; identity.md \u00a7Operations lists revokeUser's cascades without PATs) \u2014 noted for reconciliation. Harness op `revoke_user` MUST invoke only the SDK's user-revocation operation (`revokeUser`), with no extra cascade call, so the vector tests that revoking a user is sufficient. Harness op `reinstate_user` maps to `reinstateUser`.",
  "tests": [
    {
      "id": "user_status.verify_password.suspended_refused",
      "description": "A suspended user's correct password is refused.",
      "users": [],
      "steps": [
        {
          "op": "create_user_with_password_credential",
          "input": {
            "identifier": "sus@example.com",
            "password": "long-enough-password-for-floor"
          },
          "captures": {
            "usr_id": "user.id"
          }
        },
        {
          "op": "suspend_user",
          "input": {
            "usr_id": "{usr_id}"
          }
        },
        {
          "op": "verify_password",
          "input": {
            "identifier": "sus@example.com",
            "password": "long-enough-password-for-floor"
          },
          "expected": {
            "error": "InvalidCredentialError"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "user_status.verify_password.reinstated_ok",
      "description": "Known positive: suspend then reinstate; the correct password verifies.",
      "users": [],
      "steps": [
        {
          "op": "create_user_with_password_credential",
          "input": {
            "identifier": "back@example.com",
            "password": "long-enough-password-for-floor"
          },
          "captures": {
            "usr_id": "user.id"
          }
        },
        {
          "op": "suspend_user",
          "input": {
            "usr_id": "{usr_id}"
          }
        },
        {
          "op": "reinstate_user",
          "input": {
            "usr_id": "{usr_id}"
          }
        },
        {
          "op": "verify_password",
          "input": {
            "identifier": "back@example.com",
            "password": "long-enough-password-for-floor"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
